    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `AcceptanceTest` passes; `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` are a base class and helper, not tests).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipNumber` assignment formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`), following existing Spring/PetClinic conventions established by the sibling `customerCode` field:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added the `membershipNumber` field mapped to `@Column(name = \"membership_number\")` plus getter/setter.\n\n2. **Controller** (`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`) \u2014 added `assignMembershipNumber(owner)` to the `addOwner` create flow (right after `assignCustomerCode`, once `registrationDate` has been defaulted). It builds the number from the owner's own fields: `customerCode + \"-M\" + last two digits of registrationDate.getYear()` (zero-padded), so it's seed-independent.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `readOnly` `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` response schema, which generates the `OwnerDto` field that MapStruct auto-maps from the entity.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `membership_number` column to all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres); tests run on hsqldb.\n\nNo mapper change was needed \u2014 MapStruct maps `membershipNumber` (Owner\u2192OwnerDto) by name, and the create-side `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` leaves it unmapped like the existing `householdId`/`namesakeCount` targets.",
